<title>USA: Boeing signs $300 mln Aero Vodochody deal.</title>
<headline>Boeing signs $300 mln Aero Vodochody deal.</headline>
<dateline>ANAHEIM, Calif. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co said Tuesday it has signed a contract with Aero Vodochody Ltd, of the Czech Republic, to provide advanced avionics and weapon delivery systems for 72 lead-in fighter aircraft for the Czech Air Force worth about $300 million.</p>
<p>Boeing designed and developed the avionics and weapons delivery suite for the aircraft under a previous contract with Aero Vodochody.</p>
<p>The prototype aircraft was unveiled at ceremonies in the Czech Republic on June 12. The first production aircraft will be delivered to the Czech Air Force in 1999.</p>
</text>
